  "description": "ZICXES crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H126 Gd6 Mn6 N20 O60,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(C1 H4 O1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.726-3.963 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.22-122.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C128H126Gd6Mn6N20O60·4(C3H7NO)·2(CH4O)·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
